<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<section xml:id="sec-minor-extended-grid-practice" xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude">
  <title>Minor ii-V-I Keyboard Familiarisation</title>
  <p>Practice consecutive Minor ii-V-I progressions across the keyboard. In all cases the ii chord is in root position the V chord is in 2nd inversion and the I chord in root. Transition to the next ii-V-I starting each progression with the half diminished chord of the last minor 7. To be entirely accurate (chords developed from the harmonic minor scale) the i chord should be a miMaj7 but in nearly all use cases this is changed to a m7 . Practicing these progressions is useful for establishing muscle memory and an auditory memory of these important minor ii V I progression.</p>
  <pagebreak/>
  <figure xml:id="fig-minor-extended-grid-practice">
    <caption> Minor ii-V-I practice. Continue pattern through the other ii V I's</caption>
    <sbsgroup>
      <sidebyside widths="31% 31% 31%" margins="2%">
        <image xml:id="img-minor-extended-grid-practice-1">
          <latex-image>
\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=0.30, transform shape]
\pgfmathsetmacro{\isoangle}{60}
\pgfmathsetmacro{\vv}{11}
\pgfmathsetmacro{\hh}{6}
\pgfmathsetmacro{\vlen}{0.85}
\pgfmathsetmacro{\ang}{\isoangle/2}
\pgfmathsetmacro{\dlen}{(\vlen/2) / sin(\ang)}
\pgfmathsetmacro{\hlen}{(\vlen/2) / tan(\ang)}
\pgfmathsetmacro{\xmax}{\hh*\hlen}
\pgfmathsetmacro{\ymax}{\vv*\vlen}
\drawgridandnotes
\node[font=\small\bfseries] at ({\xmax/2},{11.3*\vlen}) {F$\sharp$m7$\flat$5};
\extendedgridnotes
\gn{2}{6}{F$\sharp$/G$\flat$}{1}
\gn{2}{7}{A}{1}
\gn{2}{8}{C}{1}
\gn{1}{9.5}{E}{1}
\end{tikzpicture}
          </latex-image>
